  "name": "6L6GC push-pull + output transformer + speaker (validation circuit)",
  "description": "Two 6L6GC at fixed −45 V bias and 450 V, driven anti-phase (ideal 30x drivers into 0.1 µF / 220 kΩ / 1.5 kΩ grid networks), screens via 470 Ω. Centre-tapped output transformer: 4 kΩ plate-to-plate : 4 Ω (turns 1 + 1 : 0.0632), 50 Ω and 5 mH leakage per half-primary, 0.2 Ω secondary, 16 H plate-to-plate magnetizing inductance saturating near 1.5 V·s per half-primary. Thiele–Small 4 Ω speaker load (Re 3.5 Ω, Le 0.5 mH, fs 80 Hz, Qms 4, Qes 0.6).",
  "sources": [ { "title": "N. Koren pentode model; Thiele–Small electrical equivalent (Leach, 'Introduction to Electroacoustics')" } ],
  "io": { "input": "in", "output": "spk" },
  "oversampling": 2,
